#  Death Lane

A high-speed, 2D highway survival racing web game built with vanilla JavaScript, HTML5 Canvas, and modern CSS. Dodge incoming traffic, survive the accelerating highway speed, and set a new high score!

---

##  Features

* **Advance Visuals & Graphics**: Dynamic highway asphalt with moving dash lanes, shoulder curbs, metallic gradient car textures, headlight beam projections, and smooth exhaust particle effects.
* **Auto-Speed Progression**: The game automatically increases speed every 10 seconds to keep the challenge intense.
* **Pure Web Audio API Sound System**: Built-in procedural sound generator for realistic engine rumbling pitch shifting, ignition/start chimes, and crash explosion noise effects (no external audio files required!).
* **Local High-Score Persistence**: Automatically saves and updates your best score using the browser's `localStorage`.
* **Fully Responsive / Mobile Friendly**: Optimized touch controls (Left/Right buttons) alongside traditional desktop keyboard controls (`A`/`D` or Left/Right Arrow keys).
* **Two-Stage Screen Flow**: Sleek Start Screen leading into the active gameplay arena.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **HTML5** (Structure & Canvas Rendering)
* **CSS3** (Styling, Flexbox layouts, Custom animations & gradients)
* **JavaScript (ES6)** (Game Loop, Collision Detection, Audio Synthesis, and State Management)

---

##  Project Structure

Death-Lane/

 index.html       # Main HTML file (Start screen, game HUD, canvas, touch controls)
 style.css        # Styling and layout management for mobile & desktop screens
 game.js          # Core game logic, rendering engine, audio synthesizer & controls